+/-! ### Tiling patterns of a page (task 7.3h)
+
+`loadTileLevels` finds the pattern resources the page's colours name (`patternKeys`: fills,
+strokes, glyph-run fills and strokes, inside soft masks too), loads each once by its
+`ResRef` (`Run.resLookup`), and for a tiling pattern adds the fonts of its `/Resources`
+to the font table (`Annot.loadAnnotFonts`, owner = the pattern's object, as the runner keys
+its direct fonts) before running its cell with them (`Text.textEnv`), so text in cells is laid
+out with real advances; every cell run is charged to the shared operator/form budget. The
+patterns the loaded cells use are loaded the same way, level by level, `maxPatternDepth`
+levels (the depth the painter renders). Images and shadings of cells are then loaded with the
+page's (their items carry their own `ResRef`s), glyph sources over the patterns' resources
+(`loadSourcesFrom`). -/
+
+/-- **Glyph sources of resource dictionaries** `roots` (`(owner, resources)` pairs, owner 0 the
